WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.310
Piracy and armed robbery against
ships: 137 incidents worldwide in 2025,

2
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.390
up from 116 the year before.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.050
More than half of them happened
in just one stretch of sea.

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.890
On the high seas, any state
may seize a pirate ship.

5
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.830
The sea is dangerous for others
too: people fleeing conflict,

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.850
persecution or poverty,
often in unsafe boats.

7
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.650
So why are a few stretches
of sea so dangerous?

8
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.970
Are they simply the stormiest seas?

9
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.790
In this mission, you'll
map where piracy strikes,

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.350
and how states fight back.

11
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.150
Then you'll follow sea routes
towards Europe and Australia,

12
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.370
and how they are managed.

13
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.070
Your mission: explain why a few
stretches of sea are so dangerous.
